## The Number That Actually Matters

Laser treatment does not have a single cost, and it does not have a single outcome. What it has is a real range  £500 to £1,500 out of pocket, for most patients, with no insurance support  and a real clinical record that is more mixed than the clinics advertising it will tell you.

The patients for whom laser makes the most sense are not always the ones who can most easily afford it. They are the ones for whom oral antifungal medication is off the table for medical reasons, or those who have failed it. For everyone else, the decision is financial and personal: whether the speed, convenience, and avoidance of systemic side effects is worth a meaningful premium over a £60 to £120 oral course.

What this post cannot tell you  and no post can  is which category you are in. That requires a podiatrist, a nail culture, and a genuine conversation about your health history and priorities. What it can tell you is that you now have the full picture, not a clinic's edited version of it.

